HRTF data in hrtf_data.rs
=========================

Source:   HRTF Measurements of a KEMAR Dummy-Head Microphone
          Bill Gardner and Keith Martin, MIT Media Lab Machine Listening Group, May 1994
          https://sound.media.mit.edu/resources/KEMAR.html
Archive:  https://sound.media.mit.edu/resources/KEMAR/diffuse.zip
          (the 128 point "compact" responses, equalised to the diffuse field)
Licence:  "This data is Copyright 1994 by the MIT Media Laboratory. It is provided free with no
          restrictions on use, provided the authors are cited when the data is used in any research
          or commercial application." (README of the archive; hrtfdoc.txt: "provided without any
          usage restrictions. We request that you cite the authors when using this data.")
          Attribution: Gardner, W. G. and Martin, K. D., "HRTF measurements of a KEMAR",
          J. Acoust. Soc. Am. 97(6), 3907-3908, 1995.

Used:     14 measured directions of the right hemisphere (see tools/gen_hrtf.py); the left hemisphere
          is the same data with the two ears swapped. Samples are stored exactly as measured
          (16 bit integers, 44.1 kHz) and resampled at run time to the output sample rate.
          The raw dataset is not part of this repository; regenerate with
          `python3 -I rust/aether-audio/tools/gen_hrtf.py`.
